    "summary": "An Uzbek dervish; single-page painting mounted on album folio. Uzbek dervish wearing a green kaftan with very long sleeves, red robe, white sash, yellow boots and turban with a blue cap. Blue and red purse attached to sash. Inscribed. Album contains 124 paintings of Turkish sultans and court officials.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album bound in green leather with pages of Persian paper, according to inscription. Page edges gilded with gold.",
